    "problems": "The language-forcing task uses six simple questions, and the authors say output quality and fluency, especially for lower-resource languages, remain underexplored. The study does not evaluate explanation fidelity on held-out activations, and reports no uncertainty estimates for the listed success rates.",
    "rows_left_out": "No rows were extracted for LAPE neuron counts/distributions, layerwise output analysis, downstream benchmark changes, or fallback-language patterns because these results do not measure any claim version's stated outcome. Downstream task results are described mainly in aggregate or figures.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No audit of neuron poles in Qwen3-32B or any model into one-job, two-job or not-understood shares."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "Four models (Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-Nemo-12B, Aya-Expanse-8B/32B) are studied only for language-neuron counts, layer distributions and steering. No interpretable-share estimate, no MoE models, no trillion-scale models."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No vision models, no InceptionV1 cat-and-car neuron, no test of recursive generalization versus superposition."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No comparison of interpretable-neuron shares across architectures, regularization or tools."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "No attribution graphs and no comparison with replacement models or their reconstruction error."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No test of whether explanations from activating examples predict firing elsewhere. Language labels come from activation probabilities, not inspected explanations."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "No simulation-based scoring of neuron explanations."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "All rows report the study's own steering-method performance on Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-Nemo-12B and Aya-Expanse-8B. They are correctly linked to none with state cannot_determine. The success rates were checked against Tables 1, 7 and 8 and match. The rows are method-performance results rather than claim measurements, so they belong only in fits_no_version. The Hindi/Urdu remark about 'polysemantic neurons' is unmeasured speculation and does not bear on V3 or V6. Aya-Expanse-32B has no language-forcing table, so no rows are missing for it."
